      "id": 1,
      "text": "Millersville was founded in 1761 by John Miller, who ran a blacksmith shop and hardware store.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://millersvilleborough.org/discover/about/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1854, Millersville hosted Pennsylvania’s first teachers’ academy, later becoming Millersville University.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millersville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Millersville Area Historical Society, formed in 1977, preserves artifacts, photographs, and documents of the borough’s past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/27994",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The society’s museum houses local artifacts while its research library offers books, maps, and other historical materials to the public.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/27994",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Millersville’s name evolved from Millerstown to Millersville when it was incorporated as a separate borough.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millersville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
